  "chapter": 514,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 19 Chapter 514\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8373-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the general business law and the public health law,\n        in relation to the definition of medical debt\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would align the definitions of medical debt in the General\nBusiness Law and the Public Health Law.\n \n  In December 2023, I signed Chapter 727 of  the  Laws  of  2023,  which\nprohibits  medical  debt  from  being  collected by a consumer reporting\nagency or included in a consumer report. Additionally, that law  prohib-\nits  medical providers from reporting medical debt to a consumer report-\ning agency. The law we passed last year  required  additional  technical\namendments to add a missing phrase and align certain legal definitions.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact these chang-\nes  in the upcoming legislative session. On the basis of this agreement,\nI am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2024
 },
